
Steps to Reset Activation

1. Open Command Prompt as Administrator:
	• Click the Start menu, type cmd, right-click Command Prompt, and select Run as administrator.
2. Uninstall the Current Product Key:
	• Run the following command to remove the active product key from the system registry:cmd
slmgr.vbs /upk
Use code with caution.
3. Clear Product Key Traces from Registry:
	• Run the following command to scrub the uninstalled key residue from the registry:cmd
slmgr.vbs /cpky
Use code with caution.
4. Reboot the Server:
	• Restart your computer immediately to finalize the removal:cmd
shutdown /r /t 0
Use code with caution.
5. (Optional) Extend or Rearm Grace Period:
	• If you need to reset the evaluation grace period counter (where supported), you can run:cmd
slmgr.vbs /rearm
Use code with caution.

Reapplying a New Key or Converting Editions

• To install a new product key later: Run slmgr.vbs /ipk <Your-Product-Key> followed by slmgr.vbs /ato, or navigate to Settings > System > Activation > Change product key.
• To convert from an Evaluation build to a Retail/Volume build: Use the DISM command-line tool before or alongside your key installation:cmd
DISM /online /Set-Edition:ServerStandard /ProductKey:XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX /AcceptEula
Use code with caution.
(Replace ServerStandard with ServerDatacenter if using the Datacenter edition, and reboot when prompted).